# tools/rune_assert_sweep.rish — the rune assert sweep audit.
#
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/rune_assert_sweep.rish
#
# Sweeps authored Rye for assert coverage — the TAME "say your invariants" floor:
# every function-bearing file must carry at least one assert. Per-file density
# (asserts per function) and missing `// invariant:` comments are reported as
# advisory. Seated 20260810 on Keaton's word; scoped to the Mandate module first,
# widening as more modules opt in.

say "rune-assert-sweep: Language EN — audit assert coverage across authored Rye."
say "rune-assert-sweep: Style Radiant — name each file's asserts; refuse a zero-assert module."
say "rune-assert-sweep: Lens TAME — every function-bearing file says at least one invariant."

let scan = run ["sh" "tools/fixtures/rune_assert_sweep_scan.sh" "mandate/store.rye" "mandate/keyed.rye"]
say scan.out
# values_apart: the scan's status and its verdict key must agree, so a typo'd
# sentinel cannot pass quietly.
assert scan.out contains "verdict=ok" else "rune-assert-sweep: a function-bearing file carries zero asserts"
assert scan.ok else "rune-assert-sweep: the verdict reads ok while the status fails — they must agree"

say "GREEN: rune-assert-sweep — every audited Rye file says its invariants; assert coverage swept"
